    descEn: 'In a season of drought a bedouin stood during the Friday khutbah and cried that livestock were dying and roads were cut off. The Prophet ﷺ raised his hands and prayed for rain — and rain fell for a full week. The next Friday a man begged relief from the flooding, so he prayed: "O Allah, around us, not upon us," and the clouds parted from Medina like a crown while the outskirts drank.',
